{"chunk_id": "c315ec9b4ca6", "text": "Rama, angered that the Ocean has not granted passage to Lanka, threatens to dry it up with a divine arrow. When he draws the terrifying missile\u2014likened to Brahma\u2019s rod\u2014the cosmos trembles: winds roar, mountains shake, meteors fall, and the sea surges in chaos. At last the Ocean-god Sagara rises from the waters, richly adorned and attended by great rivers, and pleads that he cannot change his nature but will aid the crossing. He advises Rama to release the unstoppable arrow elsewhere, which Rama does, blasting a distant region and creating the desert of Maru. Sagara then reveals that Nala, son of the divine architect Vishvakarma, can build a bridge. Under Nala\u2019s direction the monkey army hurls mountains, trees, and stones into the sea, constructing the vast causeway to Lanka as gods gather in awe and secretly bless Rama\u2019s campaign.\nRama threatens the ocean, forces its god to appear, then Nala builds a massive bridge enabling the monkey army to cross to Lanka.\nThemes: divine authority, nature submitting to dharma, engineering feat, war preparation, collective effort", "vector": [0.017696768045425415, -0.026989279314875603, -0.009121693670749664, 0.016917837783694267, -0.0056745815090835094, 0.014239407144486904, -0.04862169921398163, -0.003921986557543278, -0.01773776486515999, -0.03274243697524071, 0.010098773054778576, -0.005514012183994055, 0.024625156074762344, 0.010214929468929768, 0.007857638411223888, 0.005121130496263504, 0.0306379571557045, -0.020853489637374878, 0.027863869443535805, -0.011588308028876781, -0.0005504617583937943, -0.010276424698531628, 0.005138212349265814, 0.005052803084254265, -0.024761810898780823, 0.0005713869468308985, 0.024228857830166817, -0.03591282293200493, 0.010686388239264488, -0.005022055935114622, 0.004366113804280758, -0.0006452658562920988, -0.001613378175534308, 0.002979069948196411, -0.012367239221930504, -0.0008703188505023718, 0.004629173781722784, -0.004854